WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.870
Today you will learn to paint pictures with words, so your listener can see what you see.

2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:10.370
Describing words, called adjectives, tell us more about a thing.

3
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.950
A big red kite.

4
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.830
A tiny noisy puppy.

5
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.050
Think about what you can see, hear, smell, taste and feel.

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.410
The market is noisy.

7
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.100
The jalebis smell sweet.

8
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.360
Use place words to guide your listener.

9
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.720
In the middle, on the left, on the right, at the back, next to.

10
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.150
In the middle there is a tall Diwali lamp.

11
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.690
First say what the picture shows.

12
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.810
Then give three details with describing words.

13
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.990
Finally, say how it makes you feel.

14
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.170
Listen to Meera describe a Diwali picture in five sentences.

15
00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:54.210
This picture shows a family celebrating Diwali. In the middle, there are bright, golden diyas.

16
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.710
On the left, a little girl is drawing a colourful rangoli.

17
00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:06.650
At the back, I can see sparkly lights on the house. This picture makes me feel happy and excited.

18
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.960
She used place words like in the middle and on the left, and lots of describing words.

19
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.400
Listen to the difference describing words make.

20
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:19.140
Before. There is a dog. After. There is a small, fluffy, brown dog.

21
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.400
Before. The park is nice. After. The park is green, peaceful and full of tall trees.

22
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.890
Nice is a tired word. Try to choose a word that paints a clearer picture.

23
00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:35.380
You can describe places too. My favourite place is my grandmother’s garden.

24
00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:41.310
It has tall mango trees and pink flowers. I can hear birds singing in the morning.

25
00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.630
It feels calm and cool. I love it there.

26
00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.840
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

27
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.100
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
